# 2. Mutation run: each of 115 deliberate changes (first build: 98) applied alone to a scratch copy. Script: outputs/mutate-gitlab-land.mjs   Output: outputs/mutation-run.txt
$ TMPDIR=<scratch> node outputs/mutate-gitlab-land.mjs <worktree>
Baseline 58 of 58 pass on the unmutated tree. Mutations 115: caught 115, not caught 0 (first build: 98 of 98). A change counts as caught only when its text is found exactly once in the file, the changed .mjs file still parses (node --check) and the test fails or is cut by a 180 s timeout; NOOP, AMBIGUOUS, INVALID, CRASH, HUNG and SURVIVED are reported as not caught.
History: the first run of the 98 changes (against 52 cases, written before the mutations were planned) left 5 not caught: "protected file has no reason code" did not parse (the mutation was fixed), and four properties the test did not pin: a push of the reviewer that does not contain the accept, the merge-base diff of what main brings in (a branch that itself changes a governance file), the removal of the scratch worktree, and the redaction by the logger itself. A test or a mutation was added or fixed for each; the recorded run is the last.

